        <span data-field="person_name_3">{{ person_name_3 }}</span> and <span data-field="person_name_4">{{ person_name_4 }}</span>, also use EMR for upper gastrointestinal malignancies such as esophageal and stomach cancers. This added experience brings the endoscopic surgical volume at OHSU to several hundred EMRs each year. The team also expanded in the fall of 2013 with the addition of <span data-field="person_name_5">{{ person_name_5 }}</span>, from Temple University in Philadelphia, Pa., where she specialized in difficult-to-treat colorectal polyps.
      </p>

